    "body": "#### vim-patch:9.2.1097: 'splitkeep' causes a spurious scroll\r\n\r\nProblem:  When 'splitkeep' is changed after a window was split, the next\r\n          layout change moves the cursor unintentionally.\r\nSolution: Also save w_prev_winrow (Rob Pilling).\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21288\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/c71d992acdb74d706c4741a55a8579a832f7b574\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Rob Pilling <robpilling@gmail.com>",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-14T01:13:40Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Looks to be spurious/unrelated test failures\r\n\r\n<details><summary>macos intel clang oldtest</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\nExecuted:  4943 Tests\r\n Skipped:   623 Tests\r\n  FAILED:     1 Tests\r\n\r\n\r\nFailures: \r\n\tFrom test_ins_complete.vim:\r\n\tFound errors in Test_autocompletedelay_no_record():\r\n\tcommand line..script /Users/runner/work/neovim/neovim/test/old/testdir/runtest.vim[661]..function RunTheTest[61]..Test_autocompletedelay_no_record line 19:\r\nExpected 'foobar' but got 'fo'\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details><summary>windows (functional)</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\nFAILED   4 tests, listed below:\r\nExpected values to be equal.\r\nExpected:\r\n{ \"abc\", \"def\", \"ghi\" }\r\nActual:\r\n{ '      0 [main] cat (8264) C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\\\\usr\\\\bin\\\\cat.exe: *** fatal error - add_item (\"\\\\??\\\\C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\", \"/\", ...) failed, errno 1' }\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:471: in function <..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:470>\r\nFAILED   ..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua @ 476: systemlist() passing a lot of input returns the program output\r\nExpected values to be equal.\r\nExpected:\r\n{ \"01234567890ABCDEFabcdef\", ...\r\n5229Z Actual:\r\n{ '      0 [main] cat (3188) C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\\\\usr\\\\bin\\\\cat.exe: *** fatal error - add_item (\"\\\\??\\\\C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\", \"/\", ...) failed, errno 1' }\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:482: in function <..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:476>\r\nFAILED   ..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua @ 495: systemlist() with output containing NULs replaces NULs by newline characters\r\nExpected values to be equal.\r\nExpected:\r\n{ \"part1\\npart2\\npart3\" }\r\nActual:\r\n{ '      0 [main] cat (4576) C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\\\\usr\\\\bin\\\\cat.exe: *** fatal error - add_item (\"\\\\??\\\\C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\", \"/\", ...) failed, errno 1' }\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:496: in function <..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:495>\r\nFAILED   ..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua @ 501: systemlist() input passed as List joins list items with linefeed characters\r\nExpected values to be equal.\r\nExpected:\r\n{ \"line1\", \"line2\", \"line3\" }\r\nActual:\r\n{ '      0 [main] cat (8420) C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\\\\usr\\\\bin\\\\cat.exe: *** fatal error - add_item (\"\\\\??\\\\C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Git\", \"/\", ...) failed, errno 1' }\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:502: in function <..._xdg_vimscript/test/functional/vimscript/system_spec.lua:501>\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details>",
